{"version":"activity-event.v1","id":"AEV-260906-5bb3f471bc94e38884e23104","sequence":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T14:30:36.168182Z","actor":{"principal":{"availability":"unknown"},"agent":{"availability":"known","value":"claude"},"run":{"availability":"unknown"},"session":{"availability":"known","value":"42acde30-42a9-4e5e-a467-ec943234aebd"},"operator":{"availability":"unknown"}},"subject":{"element_id":"TASK-260906-vlrjo1","element_type":"task"},"source":{"kind":"local_cli","entrypoint":"cmd.runMutate","request":{"availability":"unknown"}},"correlation_id":"COR-260906-e63e04da764269eff84ad294","causal_order":1,"operation":"content","changes":[{"field":"description","before":{"kind":"text","text":""},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"environments.md 9.5 gives the dotfile-manager heuristic a closed documented list spelled only in POSIX form, so the heuristic is silently inert on Windows. Decide whether the list is platform-specific and, if it is, what each managers Windows state location is - verified on an installed binary or labelled docs-confidence, never invented."}},{"field":"scope","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define task scope)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"9.5 says: the presence of a well-known dotfile-manager state location (a closed, documented list per manager - ~/.local/share/chezmoi, ~/.config/home-manager, and the like) elevates the notice for plain unmanaged files to environment_foreign_manager_suspected. Both spellings are POSIX. chezmoi on Windows keeps its state under %LOCALAPPDATA%, a different path entirely, and home-manager is Nix-only. The curator implementation resolves the operator home portably through os.UserHomeDir and joins the listed relative paths, so the lookup is correct and the list is what makes it inert: on Windows no listed location can exist. Found by stage (c) review cycle 2 (C2-m1) after the orchestrator raised it from a windows-latest lane failure whose fixture defect was a separate matter."}},{"field":"acceptance_criteria","before":{"kind":"text","text":"(define acceptance criteria)"},"after":{"kind":"text","text":"9.5 states whether the closed list is platform-specific. If it is, each added location is either reproduced on an installed binary and recorded as verified, or labelled docs-confidence per the documents own verified/docs-confidence rule, and the manager profile and the implementation follow. If the list stays POSIX-only, 9.5 says so and says what the heuristic does on a platform where no listed location can exist, so an implementation can state a truthful bound instead of appearing to check something it cannot."}}]}
